This is my first ascension, although this has to have been the luckiest
game I have ever played since I discovered Nethack last October. I was
thoughly spoiled, however. I started this character after seeing
"Inside Man" last week, hence the name...

Notable moments of exceptional luck (thanks RGN!):

-spellbook of identify at start

-three spellbooks in Oracle's statues (!!), including magic missle (I
have found the difference between a wizard with and one w/o this spell
is often one of life and death; mm solves so many of the weaknesses of
an early wizard, allowing you to keep your distance from enemies and
attack with huge damages)

-co-alligned alter in Minetown

-Magicbane on first sacrifice (thanks to an errant dwarf in Minetown)

-wand of polymorph in mines, soon Jodie was joined by Ronald the pet
green dragon

-general store on DL4, huge potion shop on DL5 and even larger general
store on DL11 with speed boots...

-BoH in Sokoban

-blessed genocide killed all h's

-Spellbook of dig - this is a great spell, so much fun!

-Castle wand yields SDSM, magic marker, and spellbook of Magic Mapping
(this book together with dig makes the mazes go very quickly.)

-After an expensive protection racket at level 16, Jodie was Glory of
Antioch, and with it a finger of death spell

-my two stupid mistakes: She lost all protection trying to make unholy
water for nurse dancing, and later on Jodie killed Rodney with a wand
of death and the book sank in the moat! Luckily, the game had already
provided an amulet of magical breathing...

-quiet ascension run, then on Plane of Fire, Rodney shows up six times
alongside an  Archon, spawning a sea of monsters...

-surrounded by priests and insects and pestilence on Astral, Jodie
burned an amulet of life protection (and had one to spare)

-Level 22, AC -28, 348 HP at ascension

So, I am not sure what to think of this game, it just seems to have
been so lucky with equipment! A wizard with magicbane, eye of A, SDSM,
magic missle, identify, dig, magic map, and finger of death seems to be
almost a sure thing...

